WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.377
This is the executive briefing
for Book 12 of the Federal

3
00:00:04.377 --> 00:00:08.299
Modernization Workbook, Security
Operations and Telemetry.

4
00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:13.775
It's for the CISO, the SOC lead,
the CIO and authorizing officials.

5
00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:15.200
The argument is short.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.620
You can't defend what you can't see, and
the gaps that matter most make no noise:

7
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.325
a system that never sent its logs looks
exactly like one where nothing happened.

8
00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:27.600
Storing logs isn't the same
as detecting with them.

9
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.488
And a finding closes only when
the thing is fixed, with proof.

10
00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:34.725
I'll take four questions:
why, what, who and how.

11
00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:39.100
Each decision slide names the decision,
its owner and when it's needed.

12
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.660
Let's start with what a
dashboard can't show you.
